      propertyPath: m_text
      value: In ancient Egypt, scarab beetles were sacred symbols of rebirth and
        renewal, linked to the sun god Khepri. Egyptians believed both humans and
        animals had a soul that continued beyond death. This mummified beetle reflects
        their belief in life after death and the spiritual importance of all living
        creatures.
